-- title:
--   Transfer of Hecke characters from S₂(Γ₀(N)) to VₚJ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N\ge 1$ and a prime $p$. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeInputsAll N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeInputsAll.html#L8), i.e. the predicate `HeckeInputsAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N ℓ` holds for every prime $\ell$, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L25), i.e. the endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ` of the degree-zero divisor class group $J =$ [`ModularCurve.JZero N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L115) of the level-$N$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ commute pairwise; consequently the polynomial ring `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ acts on $J$ through `heckeModuleBar N`, sending $X_\ell$ to `heckeOperatorBar N ℓ`. Let $S \subseteq \mathbb N$, let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field that is a $\mathbb Q_p$-algebra, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism into $\Omega$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin 2` at primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin 2` at primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\Lambda$ from [`ModularCurve.rationalHeckeAlgebra p (ModularCurve.JZero N)`](def/ModularCurve_JZeroTateModule.html#L76), the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}$ of the rational Tate module of $J$ generated by the image of `rationalHeckeRep`, to $\Omega$ such that $\Lambda$ restricted to the scalars $\mathbb Q_p$ is the structure map $\mathbb Q_p \to \Omega$, and such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ the value of $\Lambda$ at `rationalHeckeRep p (JZero N) (heckeGen ℓ)` equals $\chi$ of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77), the class of `heckeTLin 2` at $\ell$.
--
--   This is the transfer of a weight-two Hecke eigensystem from cusp forms to the rational $p$-adic Tate module of the Jacobian, combining Eichler–Shimura compatibility of Hecke correspondences with the faithfulness of the Tate module on Hecke endomorphisms. It is used in the construction of Hecke eigenplanes in the Tate module of $J_0(N)$ and of the Galois representation attached to a weight-two eigenform.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ringHom_rationalHeckeAlgebra_extends_heckeChar.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JZeroTateModule
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_HeckeModule
